note gpu-dump.om: emit the gk and gr kernels for the small parity shape and write the whole 64-slot
note code image gkcode (16 KiB per slot, 1 MiB) to stdout and a 128-byte table to stderr: bytes 0..63
note the declared GPR counts gkgpr, bytes 64..127 the QMD TARGET_SM_CONFIG field of gksmw (hw value,
note 0 for an id with no kernel), one byte per kernel id. No GPU is touched. Compose it after the parts
note of the ollm_gb10 row of train/units.tsv with lio.om's `fn main to int` renamed (two mains
note otherwise); upstream tests/omegallm/gpu-disasm.sh fed the slots to nvdisasm and checked each
note slot's gkgpr. The image depends on the dims of grset only, not on the layer count or a loop.
global gdgpr uchar 128
fn main to int
grset 256 32 64 2 128 2
if not grall
exit 3
end
if not gkall
exit 2
end
w = write 1 gkcode 0 1048576
for i ulong 64
put gdgpr i uchar get gkgpr i
if ne get gkthr i 0
put gdgpr add i 64 uchar and shr gksmw uint i 23 63
end
end
w = write 2 gdgpr 0 128
exit 0
end
